BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Lons-le-Saunier//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Lons-le-Saunier — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vin Jaune — Savagnin aged under its veil of yeast for at least six years and three months\, sold in the 62 cl clavelin.
DESCRIPTION:Say: van ZHOHN. No other wine in France is made this way\; the clavelin is the law\, not a style. Best: Domaine Stéphane Tissot’s tasting room\, Place de la Liberté\, Arbois
LOCATION:Domaine Stéphane Tissot’s tasting room\, Place de la Liberté\, Arbois
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Domaine+St%C3%A9phane+Tissot+35+Place+de+la+Libert%C3%A9+Arbois+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Savagnin ouillé — The same grape kept in topped-up barrels: fresh\, salty\, no veil.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sah-vah-NYAN oo-YAY. Taste it beside a Vin Jaune and you learn what the veil does. Best: On the all-Jura list at La Finette\, Arbois
LOCATION:On the all-Jura list at La Finette\, Arbois
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Finette+22+avenue+Pasteur+Arbois+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ploussard — The Jura’s pale\, nearly translucent red grape\, also called Poulsard.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ploo-SAR. Pupillin\, where it grows best\, calls itself its world capital. Best: By the glass at La Table du Grapiot\, Pupillin
LOCATION:By the glass at La Table du Grapiot\, Pupillin
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Table+du+Grapiot+3+rue+Bagier+Pupillin+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Trousseau — The firmer\, darker Jura red\, with more tannin than Ploussard.
DESCRIPTION:Say: troo-SOH. The red to drink with Comté and game. Best: Domaine Stéphane Tissot’s tasting room\, Arbois
LOCATION:Domaine Stéphane Tissot’s tasting room\, Arbois
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Domaine+St%C3%A9phane+Tissot+35+Place+de+la+Libert%C3%A9+Arbois+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Macvin du Jura — Grape must stopped with Marc du Jura and aged in oak: the Jura’s apéritif.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mak-VAN. One of the region’s own appellations\, older than any rule written for it. Best: In the soufflé glacé au Macvin at La Petite Auberge\, or a glass at an Arbois cellar
LOCATION:In the soufflé glacé au Macvin at La Petite Auberge\, or a glass at an Arbois cellar
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Petite+Auberge+1985+route+de+Besan%C3%A7on+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Crémant du Jura — Sparkling wine made by a second fermentation in the bottle\, mostly Chardonnay.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kray-MAHN dew zhew-RAH. The everyday bubble of the slope\, an appellation since 1995. Best: Domaine Stéphane Tissot’s tasting room\, Arbois
LOCATION:Domaine Stéphane Tissot’s tasting room\, Arbois
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Domaine+St%C3%A9phane+Tissot+35+Place+de+la+Libert%C3%A9+Arbois+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Comté at three ages — The great cheese of the massif\, cut young\, middle-aged and old side by side.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kon-TAY. The ages taste like three cheeses\; the lesson takes five minutes at a stall. Best: The Thursday market\, Place de Verdun\, Lons
LOCATION:The Thursday market\, Place de Verdun\, Lons
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+de+Verdun+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mont d’Or — The winter cheese in its spruce box\, baked whole and spooned out hot.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mon DOR. Sold only from 10 September to 10 May: in season now. Best: The Thursday market\, Lons — a box for the galley oven
LOCATION:The Thursday market\, Lons — a box for the galley oven
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+de+Verdun+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Morbier — A supple cheese with a line of black charcoal through the middle.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mor-BYAY. The family at 39 rue du Commerce has made it for four generations. Best: Chez l’Artisan Fromager\, 39 rue du Commerce\, Lons
LOCATION:Chez l’Artisan Fromager\, 39 rue du Commerce\, Lons
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Chez+l%27Artisan+Fromager+39+rue+du+Commerce+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Saucisse de Morteau — Pork sausage smoked in a mountain chimney and closed with a wooden peg.
DESCRIPTION:Say: so-SEES duh mor-TOH. Check for the peg: it is how the real one is told from the rest. Best: The Thursday market\, Lons\, or on the plate at La Finette\, Arbois
LOCATION:The Thursday market\, Lons\, or on the plate at La Finette\, Arbois
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+de+Verdun+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cancoillotte — A runny cheese of melted skimmed-milk curd\, sold cold in jars.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kahn-kwah-YOT. Franche-Comté’s own\, and almost nowhere else\; warm it and pour. Best: The Thursday market\, Lons
LOCATION:The Thursday market\, Lons
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+de+Verdun+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Poularde au Vin Jaune et morilles — Bresse hen in a sauce of Vin Jaune\, cream and dried morels.
DESCRIPTION:Say: poo-LARD oh van ZHOHN ay mo-REE. The dish the region is built to explain. Best: La Table du Grapiot\, Pupillin\, on the longer menus\; La Finette in Arbois for the tavern version
LOCATION:La Table du Grapiot\, Pupillin\, on the longer menus\; La Finette in Arbois for the tavern version
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Table+du+Grapiot+3+rue+Bagier+Pupillin+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Croûte aux morilles — Morels in a cream and Vin Jaune sauce on toasted bread.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kroot oh mo-REE. The spring mushroom\, kept dry for the rest of the year. Best: Ô Tablier\, rue Émile Monot\, Lons — its signature
LOCATION:Ô Tablier\, rue Émile Monot\, Lons — its signature
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=O+Tablier+20+rue+Emile+Monot+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:lons-le-saunier-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Galet de Chalain — A Pelen sweet: nougatine shell\, almond-hazelnut praline\, a coat of cocoa.
DESCRIPTION:Say: gah-LAY duh shah-LAN. Named for the lake where the region’s Neolithic villages were found. Best: Pâtisserie Pelen\, 1 rue Saint-Désiré\, Lons
LOCATION:Pâtisserie Pelen\, 1 rue Saint-Désiré\, Lons
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pelen+1+rue+Saint-D%C3%A9sir%C3%A9+Lons-le-Saunier+France
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
